WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:05.670
2018 has already delivered a number of standout
horror movies, many of them flying under the

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:10.200
radar of most moviegoers - so we've collected
our favorites in this list, making it easier

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.600
than ever to find some gold in this ever-growing
content heap.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:19.080
Subtlety and style don't often rule the box
office, particularly when it comes to genre

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:23.640
fare; the horror landscape has been frequently
dominated by in-your-face slashers, squeamish

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.360
torture marathons, and gritty found-footage
outings.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:30.040
It can come as a pleasant surprise, then,
when a movie gets enough of a budget for some

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:34.290
striking visuals while remaining quiet enough
to leave you with lingering questions and

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:36.020
a genuine sense of unease.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:41.000
Alex Garland, an author and screenwriter who
made his directorial debut with the 2015 sci-fi

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.660
sleeper hit Ex Machina, returned in 2018 with
Annihilation.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:49.870
Hailed by critics with phrases like "heady
nightmare fuel," Garland's sophomore effort

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:54.880
deftly blends a metaphor-laced space invasion
story with creeping dread and uncanny imagery.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:59.149
Though it was a financial disappointment in
theaters, word of mouth has only continued

00:00:59.149 --> 00:01:02.190
to build around Annihilation since its home
video release.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:06.140
Its big ideas and its cast of fan favorite
actors ensure that it will continue to be

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:09.000
discovered by audiences for years to come.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:14.040
Humor and horror frequently rely on a similar
set of tools for surprising the audience,

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.310
and lately, comedy superstars are making that
leap with gusto.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:22.390
Jordan Peele's expertise in satirical sketches
brought Get Out to terrifying life, and Eastbound

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:27.090
and Down creators Danny McBride and David
Gordon Green blended their penchant for slapstick

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:29.420
with real scare power for Halloween.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:33.950
Between those two crossovers, The Office star
John Krasinski made an impressive turn as

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:36.400
director, co-writer, and star of A Quiet Place.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:41.150
Perhaps it was his nine seasons enduring painfully
awkward pauses at Dunder Mifflin that prepared

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:44.060
Krasinski to pull off the harrowing tension
of A Quiet Place.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:45.880
"Our prices have never been lower.”

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.030
“Son, you have to talk louder.”

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:48.340
“Never been lower!”

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:49.340
“Louder, son!”

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:50.340
“BUTTLICKER!

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:52.240
OUR PRICES HAVE NEVER BEEN LOWER!”

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:53.540
“Okay, stop it.”

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:57.229
The movie captured the attention of audiences
and critics when it crept into theaters in

00:01:57.229 --> 00:02:02.470
April, with its clever premise and minimalist
presentation that leaves much to the imagination.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:07.040
Its tiny cast is rounded out with a stellar
performance by Emily Blunt, newcomer Noah

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:11.450
Jupe, and young deaf actress Millicent Simmonds,
who made sure that the film's portrayal of

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:14.920
life for a family with a deaf child remained
authentic.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:19.560
Many of the best horror films reflect the
cultural tenor of their time, extrapolating

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:23.920
new technologies or societal shifts into speculative
tales of terror.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:28.730
Even stories that seem conceptually downright
silly can tap into frighteningly real anxieties

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:32.129
that are on the audience's mind, or will be
in the near future.

00:02:32.129 --> 00:02:36.520
Such is the case with Upgrade, a schlocky
bit of body horror that plays on the moral

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:40.890
questions surrounding artificial intelligence
and billionaire tech entrepreneurs.

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:45.819
In a not-too-distant future where computer-assisted
body modification is the norm, a mechanic

00:02:45.819 --> 00:02:51.140
named Grey remains staunchly defensive of
his own humanity, refusing to become augmented.

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:56.569
That is, until a malfunction by his self-driving
car leaves his wife dead and himself wheelchair-bound.

00:02:56.569 --> 00:03:00.650
Enter tech innovator Eron Keen, who offers
to restore Grey's motor functions with his

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:02.040
newest AI chip.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:06.940
As any horror aficionado could guess, this
melding of man and machine has some gruesome

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:07.950
results.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:12.500
Directed by Leigh Whannell of Saw fame and
produced by genre juggernaut Blumhouse, Upgrade

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:16.800
blends topical concerns with an old-fashioned
sense of gritty grindhouse fun.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:19.280
"I need your permission to operate independently.”

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:20.560
“Permission granted!”

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:21.720
“Thank you."

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:30.640
Surprisingly receptive critics have also praised
its sharp humor and tight plotting.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:36.430
Horror anthologies have a long and storied
history across a variety of media.

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:40.409
Movies have had mixed success with the format,
though, as getting audiences to sit still

00:03:40.409 --> 00:03:42.810
for two hours of short stories can be a challenge.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:47.849
After the 1980s saw the release of the cult
favorite Creepshow and the infamously disastrous

00:03:47.849 --> 00:03:53.070
Twilight Zone: The Movie, horror anthology
films went mostly dormant until recent years,

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:56.379
when Trick 'r Treat and the V/H/S series became
Halloween staples.

00:03:56.379 --> 00:04:01.989
In 2018, American audiences were treated to
an import of a new British horror anthology,

00:04:01.989 --> 00:04:02.989
Ghost Stories.

00:04:02.989 --> 00:04:07.670
The project began its life as a stage play
by Andy Nyman and Jeremy Dyson, who adapted

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:11.319
it into a film starring Nyman, Paul Whitehouse,
and Martin Freeman.

00:04:11.319 --> 00:04:16.560
The story follows a professor known for debunking
hoaxes as he investigates three cases of alleged

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:17.910
paranormal activity.

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:22.810
The lines between reality and fiction blur
as the anthology builds to a startlingly surreal

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:26.320
climax, all of which earned largely positive
reviews.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:31.639
Zombies and vampires may have had recent moments
in the sun, but werewolves are a monster vein

00:04:31.639 --> 00:04:34.599
that remains largely untapped in current pop
culture.

00:04:34.599 --> 00:04:39.419
That only adds to the joy in watching as Wildling
slowly reveals its supernatural elements while

00:04:39.419 --> 00:04:42.129
weaving a smart and sympathetic character
study.

00:04:42.129 --> 00:04:46.860
Like most classic tales of lupine transformation,
it's a coming-of-age story, designed to do

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:49.720
for young women of today what Ginger Snaps
did in 2000.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:53.480
"Ginger?”

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:02.000
The feature debut from director Fritz Böhm,
Wildling is buoyed by performances from genre

00:05:02.009 --> 00:05:06.669
favorites Liv Tyler and Brad Dourif, best
known to horror hounds as the voice of Chucky.

00:05:06.669 --> 00:05:11.319
Bel Powley takes the lead as Anna, a teenage
girl who is rescued by the local sheriff after

00:05:11.319 --> 00:05:15.599
growing up under the abusive thumb of a father
figure who claimed to be protecting her from

00:05:15.599 --> 00:05:17.899
man-eating creatures outside.

00:05:17.899 --> 00:05:22.050
Wildling has been hailed by critics for its
powerhouse performances and striking visuals.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:27.260
The Hollywood Reporter listed it as one of
the ten best films debuting at SXSW, and it's

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:30.440
definitely one of the best horror films of
2018.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:35.479
Netflix has spent the last few years ramping
up their output of original content, and the

00:05:35.479 --> 00:05:37.770
results have been mixed, to say the least.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:41.909
Freed from the need to sell tickets and relying
largely on word-of-mouth for publicity, the

00:05:41.909 --> 00:05:46.869
streaming platform's release strategies have
created a new arena of risks and surprises.

00:05:46.869 --> 00:05:51.789
For every pop culture smash like Stranger
Things, there's a misguided fizzle like Disjointed.

00:05:51.789 --> 00:05:56.169
For every big-budget disappointment like Bright,
there's a hidden gem like Cargo.

00:05:56.169 --> 00:06:00.249
With the glut of zombie fare over the past
decade, it's understandable that a drama about

00:06:00.249 --> 00:06:03.279
the walking dead might get lost in the shuffle
and shamble.

00:06:03.279 --> 00:06:07.889
Cargo, however, brings some fresh brains to
the sub-genre with a quiet story about one

00:06:07.889 --> 00:06:10.979
family's post-outbreak life in rural Australia.

00:06:10.979 --> 00:06:15.419
Directed by the filmmaking team of Ben Howling
and Yolanda Ramke and anchored by an understated

00:06:15.419 --> 00:06:19.810
but intense performance by Martin Freeman,
Cargo was favorably compared by critics to

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:22.840
the works of George A. Romero and John Hillcoat.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:28.240
A24 has established itself as a distributor
of movies by up-and-coming filmmakers who

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:32.960
are ready to balance nuanced stories with
stylish visuals, all on a small budget.

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:37.369
Their greatest success to date is probably
Barry Jenkins' Best Picture winner Moonlight,

00:06:37.369 --> 00:06:40.990
but they also secured a place in the hearts
of horror fans with The Witch and It Comes

00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:46.849
at Night - and they continued that hot streak
in 2018 with another low-key creepfest, Hereditary.

00:06:46.849 --> 00:06:51.289
The feature debut from writer/director Ari
Aster, Hereditary sets out to unnerve you

00:06:51.289 --> 00:06:56.849
with a cornucopia of disturbing omens, bizarre
visuals, and surreal nightmare logic.

00:06:56.849 --> 00:07:00.629
Critics immediately got behind it in a big
way, heaping particular praise on the lead

00:07:00.629 --> 00:07:02.479
performance by Toni Collette.

00:07:02.479 --> 00:07:08.069
Interestingly, Hereditary seems to have caused
a polarizing split between critics and audiences,

00:07:08.069 --> 00:07:12.469
as evidenced by the wide gap between its critic
and audience scores at Rotten Tomatoes.

00:07:12.469 --> 00:07:17.099
Regardless, it's been a smashing success at
the box office, having already made back its

00:07:17.099 --> 00:07:19.160
budget several times over.

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:24.469
Everyone who buys a ticket to a Nicolas Cage
vehicle knows to expect something bonkers.

00:07:24.469 --> 00:07:29.259
Even that won't prepare you for Mandy, a surreal
experience in sound, color, and vengeance.

00:07:29.259 --> 00:07:34.810
The entire cast turn in mesmerizing performances
in this second film from director Panos Cosmatos.

00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:39.399
Set in the early 1980s, Mandy is the story
of a man taking violent revenge against a

00:07:39.399 --> 00:07:42.819
religious cult and the supernatural forces
allied with them.

00:07:42.819 --> 00:07:47.409
But recounting the plot of Mandy doesn't really
tell you anything about why it works.

00:07:47.409 --> 00:07:52.529
On paper, it's a fairly cliched revenge story,
but Cosmatos' style elevates the movie to

00:07:52.529 --> 00:07:54.150
a mythic, hypnotic level.

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:58.750
The movie builds to a fevered climax, immersing
us in its heroes' heavy metal and fantasy

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:00.520
novel-inspired worldview.

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:04.310
Really, nothing we could say here would explain
why critics loved Mandy.

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:06.840
You're just going to have to experience it
for yourself.

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:13.400
The word "risky" doesn't often apply to long-running
franchises, but 2018's Halloween had no right

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:15.279
to be as successful as it was.

00:08:15.279 --> 00:08:20.449
Though masked murderer Michael Myers remains
a towering horror icon, John Carpenter's 1978

00:08:20.449 --> 00:08:25.129
original is the only movie in the series to
hold unquestioned classic status.

00:08:25.129 --> 00:08:30.319
Its four-decade run has been rife with multiple
retcons, reboots, and a general sense of diminishing

00:08:30.319 --> 00:08:31.319
returns.

00:08:31.319 --> 00:08:35.279
From Eastbound and Down's Danny McBride and
David Gordon Green, the newest iteration of

00:08:35.279 --> 00:08:39.529
Halloween had a troubled road of its own,
but fans' interest was piqued when Carpenter

00:08:39.529 --> 00:08:41.909
came on board as producer and composer.

00:08:41.909 --> 00:08:46.100
The hype intensified when Jamie Lee Curtis
signed on to reprise her star-making role

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:47.240
as Laurie Strode.

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:51.170
Things were shaping up, but with a writer
and director team more versed in comedy than

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:54.310
horror, it was still hard to guess what we
were in for.

00:08:54.310 --> 00:08:58.830
What we got was a lean, thrilling sequel that
eschewed complicated slasher lore in favor

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:00.980
of a story about time and trauma.

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:05.129
Rather than put Michael front and center,
the movie makes his killing spree the backdrop

00:09:05.129 --> 00:09:08.480
to Laurie's fractured relationships with her
daughter and granddaughter.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:12.459
When the Shape does strike, though, he's as
clever and brutal as ever.

00:09:12.459 --> 00:09:16.149
Audiences and critics got behind the revival
in a big way, proving that this Halloween

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:20.000
was at last a worthy successor to its legendary
namesake.

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:25.480
With J.J. Abrams' Bad Robot production company
behind it, audiences could be forgiven for

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:29.589
suspecting that Overlord might turn out to
be a stealth Cloverfield movie.

00:09:29.589 --> 00:09:33.230
Even when Abrams denied the connection during
the film's production, it still seemed like

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:35.250
yet another bit of deception.

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:38.550
It wasn't, though - Overlord isn't a Cloverfield
movie.

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:39.740
No, really.

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:44.690
It does, however, have a traditional Abrams-style
mashup of human drama with supernatural horror.

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:49.850
The movie follows a platoon of Allied soldiers
in World War II who encounter a Nazi laboratory

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:51.889
full of horrifying creatures.

00:09:51.889 --> 00:09:56.279
Critics appreciated its skilled blend of war
movie and horror movie tropes, with one reviewer

00:09:56.279 --> 00:10:00.920
comparing Overlord favorably to Night of the
Living Dead and declaring it a future cult

00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:01.920
classic.

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:07.840
Horror remakes don't often achieve prestige
status, but that certainly happened in 2018

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:08.930
with Suspiria.

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:14.100
Call Me By Your Name director Luca Guadagnino
completely reimagined Dario Argento's 1977

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:19.150
cult favorite, twisting its bones into a deep
meditation on themes like identity, manipulation,

00:10:19.150 --> 00:10:20.920
loss, and rebellion.

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:25.960
It even threads the very idea of being a "remake"
into its own story, as dance student Susie

00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:30.100
is slowly and irreversibly changed by her
efforts to follow in the footsteps of her

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:32.360
enigmatic instructor, Madame Blanc.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:35.879
The response to Guadagnino's film has been
nothing short of polarized.

00:10:35.879 --> 00:10:40.130
A glance at Rotten Tomatoes reveals a critical
opinion resting comfortably in the middle

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:41.130
percentages.

00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:45.431
Unlike many films with such a lukewarm average,
though, Suspiria landed there because of a

00:10:45.431 --> 00:10:51.000
hard split between individual reviewers - people
either really loved it or very much did not.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:55.470
A discerning crowd at the Cannes Film Festival
gave its premiere a rousing ovation, but there's

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:59.050
no shortage of critics quite literally calling
it garbage.

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:04.410
Suspiria may well either be a horror fan's
favorite or least favorite film of 2018, but

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:09.069
the passionate reaction it's inspired certainly
suggests it won't be forgotten any time soon.

